"""Read-only middleware API. All business operations use POST /graphql."""
type Query {
  """Return ranked candidates from Monarch. The frontend/user chooses the intended concept."""
  terms(
    """Trimmed search text, 1–200 Unicode characters."""
    query: String!
    """Page size: 1–100. A value outside that range is rejected, not clamped."""
    limit: Int! = 20
    """Zero-based offset: 0–10000."""
    offset: Int! = 0
  ): TermResults

  """
  Type-ahead suggestions for a partially typed term, each annotated with what BDC holds, plus
  the BDC variables matching the text.

  Both operations attach transformation metadata. Study counts describe mapping specifications.

  No limit or offset: the upstream autocomplete route accepts only the query, so the suggestion
  list is as long as it chooses to make it and cannot be sized or paged. For a longer, paginated
  list use `terms`.
  """
  autocomplete(
    """Partially typed text, 1–200 Unicode characters."""
    query: String!
  ): AutocompleteResults

  """Process status; does not load YAML or contact Monarch. Use Actuator for probes."""
  health: Health!
}
"""One page, in Monarch's relevance order. An empty page is a successful result."""
type TermResults {
  """
  One page, in display order: harmonized BDC variables first, then knowledge-graph concepts.

  A single list on purpose. Variables and concepts were once returned separately, which left
  the client merging them and broke paging — twenty concepts plus three pinned variables is
  twenty-three rows. Here `limit` means what it says: ask for twenty, get twenty.

  Variables sit at the front of the whole result set, not of each page. With three matching
  variables, the first twenty are 3 variables + 17 concepts and the next twenty are concepts
  18–37. Nothing is repeated or skipped; page on `offset` alone.

  Resolve with inline fragments — see SearchItem.
  """
  items: [SearchItem!]!
  """BDC variables plus the provider's concept total, so it counts what `items` counts."""
  total: Int!
  """The page size actually applied."""
  limit: Int!
  """The offset actually applied."""
  offset: Int!
  """Whether a further page exists. Use this rather than arithmetic on `total`."""
  hasMore: Boolean!
  """
  How many of `total` are harmonized variables. Lets you label the pinned section without
  counting `__typename` yourself.
  """
  bdcVariableCount: Int!
}
"""A biomedical concept from the knowledge graph, with whatever BDC holds for it."""
type Term {
  """The concept's CURIE, e.g. MONDO:0005044. The only guaranteed field, the value you carry
  forward when the user selects, and the key every BDC annotation is joined on."""
  id: ID!
  """Primary name from the knowledge graph."""
  label: String!
  """Biolink category, e.g. biolink:Disease. The main axis for telling a disease from a phenotype."""
  category: String!
  """Null when the knowledge graph holds no description. Null means absent, not empty."""
  description: String
  """Alternative names. Null means not supplied; [] means known to have none."""
  synonyms: [String!]
  """`label (id)`, computed so every surface identifies a concept identically."""
  displayLabel: String!
  """What BDC has harmonized for this concept. Never null; zero when nothing is harmonized."""
  bdc: BdcCoverage!
}

"""Suggestions for a partially typed term. Unpaginated: the upstream route takes only `q`."""
type AutocompleteResults {
  """
  Suggestions in display order: harmonized BDC variables first, then concepts. The same shape as
  TermResults minus the paging fields, so one code path renders both operations.
  """
  items: [SearchItem!]!
  """BDC variables plus the provider's reported total."""
  total: Int!
  """How many of `items` are harmonized variables."""
  bdcVariableCount: Int!
}

"""
An entry in a result list: either a harmonized BDC variable or a knowledge-graph concept.

They are genuinely different things — one has studies and a domain, the other an ontology
category and synonyms — so they are a union rather than one type with half its fields null.
Select with inline fragments and branch on `__typename`:

```
items {
__typename
... on BdcVariable { name label domain studyCount studies concepts }
... on Term { id label category description displayLabel bdc { studyCount studies } }
}
```
"""
union SearchItem = BdcVariable | Term


"""
What BDC has harmonized for one concept.

Describes harmonization specifications, not participant data: three studies means three studies
wrote a rule for this concept, not that any dataset is accessible. Zero also means zero when the
index is switched off, so do not render it as "BDC has nothing".
"""
type BdcCoverage {
  """Distinct studies whose specifications assign this exact concept."""
  studyCount: Int!
  """Those studies by name, e.g. ["ARIC", "FHS"]."""
  studies: [String!]!
  """
  Names of the variables that assign it. Look them up in the operation's `bdcVariables` list for
  the full record; they are names here so the same type does not appear in two places meaning
  two different things.
  """
  variableNames: [String!]!
}

"""
A variable harmonized across BDC studies.

A deliberately small view, read from files vendored from the harmonization repository. The
source carries much more — dbGaP accessions, BDCHM classes, data types, units, definitions —
and any of it can be added later without breaking a client.
"""
type BdcVariable {
  """Machine name from the specification files, e.g. "hyperten". Unique and stable; use as a key."""
  name: String!
  """Human-readable name, e.g. "Hypertension". Falls back to `name`, so it is never null."""
  label: String!
  """Coarse grouping, e.g. "DIAGNOSIS", "MEASUREMENT", "MEDICATION". Null when not categorised."""
  domain: String
  """How many studies harmonize this variable."""
  studyCount: Int!
  """Those studies by name."""
  studies: [String!]!
  """Ontology CURIEs its specifications assign, e.g. ["MONDO:0005044"]."""
  concepts: [String!]!
}

type Health { service: String!, status: String! }
